    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, can you look at these logs? We're getting weird intermittent packet loss on the 192.168.45.0/24 subnet here in Lyon. Traceroutes are showing huge spikes in jitter at the third hop.\n\nhop 1: 10.0.0.1 (lat: 1ms)\nhop 2: 172.16.5.1 (lat: 2ms)\nhop 3: 192.168.45.1 (lat: 150ms, 450ms, 310ms, 2ms)\nhop 4: 203.0.113.5 (lat: 12ms)\n\nPing test shows 5% loss over a 100-packet burst. Is this likely a hardware issue at the gateway or just congestion?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
